    "value": "315"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12b-2009-p12.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The eighth term divided by the fifth term is \\(r^3 = \\dfrac{8!}{7!} = 8,\\) so \\(r = 2.\\)\n\nThe fifth term is \\(a r^4 = 7!,\\) so \\(a = \\dfrac{7!}{16} = \\dfrac{5040}{16} = 315.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "The ratio of the eighth term to the fifth term is \\(r^3\\)",
        "\\(\\dfrac{8!}{7!} = 8 = r^3,\\) so \\(r = 2\\); then divide \\(7!\\) by \\(r^4\\)"
      ],
